-- title:
--   A q'-new eigenform congruent to χ₁ modulo 𝔪
-- statement:
--   Fix $M\ge 1$ and a natural number $q'$, and an Atkin–Lehner datum $A$ for $q'$ at level $M$, that is, a factorisation $M=q'R$ together with integers $a,b$ satisfying $q'a-Rb=1$; assume $q'$ is prime. Let $\mathfrak m$ be a maximal ideal of the ring $\overline{\mathbf Z}$ of algebraic integers in $\mathbf C$, and let $\chi_1$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ M}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\overline{\mathbf Z}$; here $\mathbb T$ is the $\mathbf Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbf C}S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$ (the excluded set $\{\ell\mid \ell\mid M\}$ removes all $U_q$ generators). Assume the support hypothesis: every $T\in\mathbb T$ whose associated endomorphism kills every element of $\ker(\mathrm{Tr}_A)\cap\ker(\mathrm{Tr}_A\circ w_{q'})$ lies in $\chi_1^{-1}(\mathfrak m)$, where $\mathrm{Tr}_A=$ [`CuspForm.traceLin A hq'`](def/CuspForm_LevelLoweringTrace.html#L18) sends $f$ to $f+U_{q'}(f\,|\,W)$ in $S_2(\Gamma_0(R))$ and $w_{q'}=$ [`CuspForm.atkinLehnerLin A 2`](def/CuspForm_AtkinLehnerOperator.html#L41) is the Atkin–Lehner involution attached to $A$. The conclusion is that there exists $g\in S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ which is a normalised eigenform in the sense of `IsNormalizedEigenform` ($a_1(g)=1$, multiplicativity of $a_n$ at coprime indices, and the two prime-power recursions according as $p\nmid M$ or $p\mid M$), which satisfies $a_{q'}(g)^2=1$, and which is congruent to $\chi_1$ modulo the same $\mathfrak m$: for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ the coefficient $a_\ell(g)$ is the image of an algebraic integer $b$ with $\chi_1(T_\ell)-b\in\mathfrak m$.
--
--   This is the Deligne–Serre style passage from a Hecke-algebra support statement to an actual $q'$-new normalised eigenform, strengthened so that the congruence holds modulo the given maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ rather than modulo some prime of the Hecke algebra; the adjustment is made by replacing $g$ by a suitable $\mathrm{Aut}(\mathbf C)$-conjugate. It feeds the level-raising step, being used by [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_isNewAt_congr_of_levelRaisingCongruence`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_isNewAt_congr_of_levelRaisingCongruence).
